{"id":"word:hebrew:H898","type":"word","title":"בָּגַד","subtitle":"H898 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to cover (with a garment); figuratively, to act covertly ; by implication, to pillage","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בָּגַד (H898) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 49 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בָּגַד (bâgad) means to cover (with a garment); figuratively, to act covertly ; by implication, to pillage First listed occurrence: 1Sam 14 33."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בָּגַד","transliteration":"bâgad","pronunciation":"baw-gad'","strong":"H898","lemmaId":"hebrew:H898","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["בֹּגְדִ֣ים","בָּגָ֔דוּ","בָּ֣גְדוּ","וּ֝/בוֹגְדִ֗ים","בְּגַדְתֶּ֔ם"],"morphs":[["HVqrmpa",9],["HVqp3cp",9],["HVqrmsa",5],["HVqp2mp",2],["HVqa",2],["HVqp3fs",2],["HVqrmpc",2],["HC/Vqw3mp",2],["HC/Vqrmpa",2],["HR/Vqc/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to cover (with a garment); figuratively, to act covertly ; by implication, to pillage","usage":"deal deceitfully (treacherously, unfaithfully), offend, transgress(-or), (depart), treacherous (dealer, -ly, man), unfaithful(-ly, man), × very.","full":"H898. bagad [ בָּגַד ] verb act or deal treacherously — Qal Perfect בָּֽגְדָה Jer 3:20 14 t.; Imperfect יִבְגֹּד Mal 2:15 5 t.; נִבְגַּד 2:10 ; Infinitive absolute בָּגוֺד Isa 48:8 ; Jer 5:11 ; construct בְּגֹד Isa 33:1 ; בִּגְדוֺ Exod 21:8 ; Participle בֹּגֵד Prov 22:12 11 t.; בּוֺגֵד Isa 33:1 10 t.; — act or deal treacherously, faithlessly, deceitfully , in the marriage relation, in matters of property or right, in covenants, in word and in General conduct. a. absolute 1Sam 14:33 ; Job 6:15 ; Psa 78:57 ; Isa 24:16 ; 33:1 (twice in verse); 48:8 ; Mal 2:11 . compare phrases נחל כמו בגדו אחי my brethren have dealt deceitfully as a brook Job 6:15 ; בָּגָ֑דוּ בּוֺגְדִים וּבֶגֶד בָּנָ֑דוּ בֹּגְדִים the treacherous have dealt treacherously, yea in treachery have the treacherous dealt treacherously Isa 24:16 (striking alliteration); אָוֶן בֹּגְדֵי treacherous in wickedness Psa 59:6 . b. with בְּ Exod 21:8 (E), Judg 9:23 ; Isa 33:1 (twice in verse); Jer 3:20 ; 5:11 ; 12:6 ; Lam 1:2 ; Hosea 5:7 ; 6:7 ; Mal 2:10 , 14 , 15 , 16 . c. with accusative Psa 73:15 . d. with מִן pregnant, מֵרֵעָהּ אִשָּׁה בָּֽגְדָה acteth treacherously (in departing) from her friend Jer 3:20 . The participle is used Prov 2:22 8 t., Psa 25:3 ; 59:6 ; 119:158 ; Isa 21:2 ; 24:16 (twice in verse); 33:1 ; Jer 3:8 , 11 ; 9:1 ; Hab 1:13 ; 2:5 ; בָ֑גֶד בֹּגְדֵי dealers treacherously in treachery (very treacherously ) Jer 12:1 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 14 33","keyReferences":["1Sam 14 33","Exod 21 8","Hab 1 13","Hab 2 5","Hos 5 7","Hos 6 7","Isa 21 2","Isa 21 2"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":49,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 14 33","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּגַדְתֶּ֔ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp2mp"},{"reference":"Exod 21 8","book":"Exod","chapter":21,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/בִגְד/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vqc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Hab 1 13","book":"Hab","chapter":1,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בּֽוֹגְדִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmpa"},{"reference":"Hab 2 5","book":"Hab","chapter":2,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בּוֹגֵ֔ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsa"},{"reference":"Hos 5 7","book":"Hos","chapter":5,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּגָ֔דוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3cp"},{"reference":"Hos 6 7","book":"Hos","chapter":6,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ֥גְדוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3cp"},{"reference":"Isa 21 2","book":"Isa","chapter":21,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/בּוֹגֵ֤ד","source"